## Credibility markers — priority order

Build the site so these are visible immediately. They compress seniority the fastest.

**Tier 1 (must be above the fold):**
- Recognisable employers and institutions
- Concrete specialisation
- Public proof artifacts — papers, code, talks
- Scope verbs: *led, owned, shipped, deployed, validated, managed, architected*
- Consistency across website / LinkedIn / GitHub / Scholar

**Tier 2 (on-page, easily reachable):**
- Selected publications and venues
- Testimonial from credible operator or researcher
- Awards, grants, invited talks
- Writing quality (the site itself is a signal)

**Tier 3 (present but secondary):**
- Professional photo
- Languages
- Location

## Copywriting patterns

Use these structures. They are grounded in what works for senior technical / clinical AI candidates.

| Pattern | Formula |
|---|---|
| Identity | `I help [org type] solve [high-value problem] using [credible domain combination].` |
| Seniority | `I work at the intersection of [A], [B], and [C], with experience spanning [research] to [deployment/validation].` |
| Flagship project | `At [org], I [owned/led/built] [system/program], helping [stakeholder] achieve [outcome] under [constraint].` |
| Credibility compression | `[current senior role] + [technical niche] + [clinical/regulated context] + [prior cross-border work]` |

**Use**: led, designed, validated, translated, built, deployed, coordinated, published
**Avoid**: revolutionised, transformed healthcare, visionary, passionate, world-class, robust, transformative

