## SEO

**Architecture**: strong homepage + small number of supporting pages (publications, biosignals, neuroimaging, medical device AI) — not pure one-pager.

**Title tag**: `Christos Zacharopoulos | Clinical AI Research Leader | Biosignals, Neuroimaging, Medical ML`

**Meta description**: `Clinical AI research leader and PhD scientist working across biosignals, neuroimaging, biomedical NLP, and regulated medical machine learning.`

**Keyword hierarchy**:
- Primary (H1): Clinical AI Research Leader
- Secondary (body): biosignal machine learning, neuroimaging ML, biomedical NLP, regulated medical AI, multimodal biomedical data
- Tertiary (project summaries): EEG/ECG biomarkers, cardiac ultrasound AI, FDA/CE MDR validation, SEPARATE, INSPECT

**Technical**:
- JSON-LD `Person` / `ProfilePage` schema with `sameAs` links (LinkedIn, GitHub, Google Scholar, ORCID)
- Descriptive `<title>` and `<meta description>` per page
- Canonical URL
- Key content in crawlable HTML — not JS-only
- XML sitemap
- Internal links between homepage, publications, and project pages

## Content constraints — strict

**Do not include:**
- Confidential clinical data or raw patient data
- Proprietary ML pipeline details or internal model architectures
- Internal regulatory documents or unpublished submission materials
- Company-owned IP or internal performance metrics not already in public abstracts
- Anything not already publicly available

When in doubt, describe the domain and the type of work, not the specifics.

